  "abstract": "This paper introduces a new six-compartment fuzzy fractional-order epidemic model that describes the spread and mitigation of math-phobia in student populations. The susceptible $Ş(t)$, mathphobic $M(t)$, not interested $N(t)$, intervention-aware $₳(t)$, interested $ƚ(t)$, and recovered $Ɍ(t)$ compartments capture key behavioural transitions influenced by psychological, social, and educational factors. Caputo-type fuzzy fractional differential equations are used to derive these dynamics, considering memory effects and epistemic uncertainty in the transmission and recovery rates. By applying fixed-point theory, we prove the existence and uniqueness of the solution under fuzzy initial conditions, hence guaranteeing mathematical coherence of the model.",
